title: 'Westend AH and People: configurable validator inactivity, StakingOperator session keys'
doc:
- audience: [Runtime Dev, Runtime User]
  description: |-
    Follow-ups to #13464 for deploying validator-collators on Westend.

    Asset Hub Westend replaces `pallet_staking_async::AllZero` with its own `IsValidatorInactive`,
    which reads the `IsValidatorInactiveThresholds` storage parameter,
    `Option<(min_relay_consensus, min_collation)>`. With `Some`, a validator is inactive in an era
    if it earned fewer relay consensus points than the first value or fewer collation points than
    the second. The default is `None`: no validator is inactive, so `chill_inactive` chills no one
    until Root sets the parameter with `System::set_storage` at
    `twox_128(":IsValidatorInactiveThresholds:")`. Benchmarks use `Some((1, 1))`, so that a
    validator with no points is inactive.

    The Asset Hub Westend `StakingOperator` proxy can also call `Session::set_keys` and
    `Session::purge_keys`, to manage the session keys with which a validator collates on Asset
    Hub, next to the relay chain keys it already managed through `StakingRcClient`.

    People Westend gains a `StakingOperator` proxy type, encoded as index 6. It can call
    `Session::set_keys`, `Session::purge_keys` and the `Utility` batch calls (`batch`,
    `batch_all`, `force_batch`), and nothing else. `NonTransfer` is a superset of it.
crates:
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: people-westend-runtime
  bump: major
